From 10f890cfd1572147c18abc4b0a0078b4fc167e0a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 14 Aug 2026 18:02:09 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] feat(seo): remove cloaking, add SharkPay keyword guides
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Ports the cleaned-up ShowPay SEO structure to SharkPay. Login form,
design and workflow are unchanged: the first screen is pixel-identical
(verified 0/1,316,640 pixels changed at 390x844) and no JS, admin-app,
supabase or vercel.json file was touched.

Cloaking removed (the main threat to the current #1 ranking):
- public/{about-sharkpay,sharkpay-apk,sharkpay-support,sharkpay-usdt}.html
  each shipped `body { opacity:0; display:none; visibility:hidden }` plus
  `setTimeout(() => location.replace("/"), 3)`. Googlebot saw keyword text,
  users saw nothing and were bounced to /. That is textbook cloaking and
  sneaky redirect, and it is what cost the sister site its rankings. The
  repo already carries a commit about a Google Safe Browsing warning.
- seo-generator.cjs injected that same cloakHead into every page it wrote.

Replaced with 9 real guides at the site root (SharkPay serves static from
the repo root, so pages must live there to resolve at /name.html):
about, apk, usdt, support, guide hub, how-to-use, how-to-deposit,
how-to-deposit-usdt, password-help. ~1000 words each, visible content,
self-contained styles, canonical + OG + JSON-LD per page.

Homepage: adds the guide content below the login screen (visible on
scroll only), a canonical tag, and an extended JSON-LD graph
(WebSite/Organization/WebPage/WebApplication/FAQPage) with the
"Sharkpay" and "Shark pay" spelling variants. Title and meta description
are deliberately left untouched — that page already ranks #1.

Also fixes the sitemap: it listed /about-sharkpay.html etc. while the
files sat under /public/, so every entry 404'd. Now lists all 10 live
URLs. robots.txt keeps the /sharkpay-admin/ disallow.
